  "summary": "SparroWocky is the modular C++ backdoor that replaced SparrowDoor as FamousSparrow's flagship implant, deployed since at least August 2025 against governmental targets in Latin America. It is delivered by a trident loader (legitimate EXE plus side-loaded malicious DLL) that RC4-decrypts a .dat payload, uses TLS with RC4-encrypted command data over IP-based C2, and persists via a Windows service or a Run key. The backdoor supports command execution, in-memory PE and BOF loading, TCP proxying, screenshots and file exfiltration, with heavy anti-analysis (SilentMoonwalk, API hashing, LDR forging).",
